    {
      "id": "e8639ae1-31fa-44b6-b627-fe458b63b02f",
      "label": "Trade Features & Foci",
      "rows": [
        {
          "columns": [
            {
              "sections": [
                {
                  "id": "c66dacfc-c2cc-45dc-8a2e-9caac8b0b30a",
                  "label": "Trade Features",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "id": "850dbe2f-d29b-4cb6-a353-4f5775926bb5",
                      "label": "Tasteful Magic",
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": "Artists have access to spells from the artistry list and learn 2 spells at level 1. They can change one of these learnt spells when levelling up. Artists use the charm trait for their casting related rolls.",
                      "meta": {
                        "helperText": ""
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "c56ec0cc-e21f-4bfb-905d-e69c668f349d",
                      "label": "Misdirection",
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": "Your natural ability to pull focus and make yourself the centre of attention allows you to be a wonderful distraction. As an action, you may dance, sing or otherwise perform to draw the attention of a combatant away from one of your allies. Make a d20 + 3 roll against the combatant's will + instinct. On a success, that combatant is distracted by your performance and all allies roll against that combatant upsized until the start of your next turn.",
                      "meta": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "47b49722-3632-47f7-a943-d7f2cc4ed2b1",
                      "label": "Beautiful Form",
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": "There is an air of artistry about yourself, down to your very movements. Whenever you make a roll that calls for panache, grace or guile, you may roll a d12 instead of the dice you would usually roll.",
                      "meta": {}
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "458fafef-117a-4cab-bf12-6357c87cca07",
                  "label": "Foci",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "id": "236f9c19-be6c-4cf0-b220-0cbe2960d244",
                      "label": "Defence",
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": "You are positioned to defend yourself from any incoming attacks. You upsize your dice for any guard or dive roll made until your next turn\n",
                      "meta": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "4c348790-0d94-4b64-a89d-b77d625c9750",
                      "label": "Offence",
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": "You are keenly aware of any opportunity to catch a foe unprepared. If a combatant attacks a combatant other than yourself while within your currently wielded melee weapons range or leaves your weapons range you may make a single weapon attack against that combatant.\n\r\n",
                      "meta": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "bcffca4f-db75-420c-850a-707c0d738ad2",
                      "label": "Details",
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": "Your well trained eye can spot swells of magic moments before they coalesce as spells. You gain the focus option \"details\". When you declare details as your focus for a turn, anytime a combatant casts a spell you can shout or otherwise communicate a warning, if able to communicate in some way, to that spell's target. Any target's of the spell warned by you, including yourself, can upsize any roll made to resist the effects of the spell, or upsize their dive or guard roll against the spell.",
                      "meta": {}
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "98c7904d-9260-48a8-b39e-e82553b91eaf",
      "label": "Species & Background",
      "rows": [
        {
          "columns": [
            {
              "sections": [
                {
                  "id": "7e9a683b-7087-4a7a-ab62-194c90e853b1",
                  "label": "Species",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "id": "8e38cd8f-34a7-42fb-a660-979302022f57",
                      "label": "Description",
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": "Elves are typically between 1.5 and 2.5 metres tall, weighing between 50 and 150kg. Like humans, they have two hands with opposable thumbs making them good tool and weapon users as well as being excellent climbers. Their lives are long leading some to hoard knowledge and value secrecy, while others cannot remain in the present moment thinking about far off futures.",
                      "meta": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "18a13dfa-cecf-468c-8afe-d966d7a840d8",
                      "label": "Habitat",
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": "Terrestrial",
                      "meta": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "8b01f13b-686a-4578-9253-1ff8dc94a9b1",
                      "label": "Attributes",
                      "type": "Text",
                      "value": "Treetop Natives (1 point)\nYour species has built homes among the canopies of large trees and live comfortably among the foliage.\n- You can climb trees and other natural surfaces such as stone at your normal land pace\n- You upsize your dice on any finesse check made to maintain balance on a high surface, leap between two surfaces, or stop yourself midfall\n\nEnduring (1 point)\nYour species has a vastly extended lifespan and looks into the far future to consider the implications of their actions well down the line.\n- You add your forethought twice to any forethought roll aside from damage rolls.\n\nToolworker (2 points)\nYour species developed complex tools to supplement their abilities.\n- You are adept with two tools from the tool list or expert with one;\n- Additionally you upsize your dice for any tool check, you upsize an additional time if you are an expert with that tool\n\nGifted (1 points)\nYour species is in tune with the arcane waves.\n- You know a spell of your choice with mana cost of exactly 1. This spell is in addition to those granted by your trade.\n- Add 1d4 to your recovery pool\n\nAttractive (1 point)\nYour species has beguiling quality that others respect, revere, and/or admire.\n- When you make a charm + panache roll, you upsize your dice and may treat your looks as a tool with which you are an expert.",
                      "meta": {}
